{"qid":"Q214","names":["Slovakia"],"title":"Slovakia","endonym":{"native":"Slovenská republika","lang":"sk"},"capsule":"Slovakia (Slovensko) is a Central European republic that became fully independent on 1 January 1993 following the peaceful dissolution of Czechoslovakia. Bratislava is its capital. It joined the European Union and NATO in 2004 and adopted the euro in 2009. It is the eastern successor of the former Czechoslovak federation, distinct from the Czech Republic.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":"place/Slovakia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Slovakia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q725803","name":"Ján Čarnogurský","start":1991,"end":1992,"image":"Ján Carnogurský (2013) 5697.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/J%C3%A1n%20Carnogursk%C3%BD%20(2013)%205697.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Pelz","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q356990","name":"Michal Kováč","start":1993,"end":1998,"image":"Michal Kováč.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Michal%20Kov%C3%A1%C4%8D.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Bodajozef","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q705654","name":"Jozef Moravčík","start":1994,"end":1994,"image":"Jozef Moravčík.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jozef%20Morav%C4%8D%C3%ADk.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"European Comission","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q